**[Suggestion]** Missing negative test for the `event.detail !== 0` guard in `handleClick` — Failure scenario: a future refactor removes the guard. In hold mode, if `setPointerCapture` fails (try/catch best-effort) on a specific browser/device and both `pointerdown` and `click` reach the handler, `start()` fires twice — once from `handlePointerDown` and once from `handleClick`. No existing test pins this guard: the "holds to start" test dispatches `click` after `pointerup`, but `pointerdown` already called `start()` and the assertion only checks `stop`.

```suggestion
