discussion_comments.comment_body:
**[Suggestion]** No test verifies that pointer events (`pointerdown`/`pointerup`/`pointercancel`) are ignored when the voice mode is `'tap'`. The existing tap-mode test only exercises click behavior.

Failure scenario: if the `voiceGate.mode !== 'hold'` guard were removed from any of the three pointer handlers, tap mode would respond to hold gestures — pressing down would start dictation, and releasing would call `stop()`, bypassing click-to-toggle. The existing tap-mode test would still pass because it only tests clicks.

Consider adding a test that renders in tap mode and verifies `pointerdown` does not start capture:

```tsx
it('ignores pointer hold in tap mode', async () => {
  mocks.workspaceVoice.mockResolvedValue(
    voiceStatus(true, '/tmp/workspace', 'tap'),
  );
  const button = await render(false);
  pointer(button, 'pointerdown');
  expect(mocks.capture.start).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
});
```

<details>
<summary>中文说明</summary>

没有测试验证当语音模式为 `'tap'` 时指针事件（`pointerdown`/`pointerup`/`pointercancel`）会被忽略。现有的 tap 模式测试仅覆盖了点击行为。

失败场景：如果从任何指针处理函数中移除 `voiceGate.mode !== 'hold'` 守卫，tap 模式将响应 hold 手势——按下会启动录音，释放会调用 `stop()`，绕过点击切换设计。现有的 tap 模式测试仍会通过，因为它只测试点击。

建议添加一个在 tap 模式下渲染并验证 `pointerdown` 不会启动捕获的测试。

</details>

